GLOSSARY = [
 ('Agent identity', 'A credential or account that an AI agent uses, kept separate from any person\'s login.'),
 ('Attestation', 'A signed statement, usually by an owner, that something is true. In the lab it was text and was not checked.'),
 ('Blast radius', 'How much damage a credential can do if it is stolen or misused.'),
 ('Break-glass account', 'An emergency account used when normal sign-in is down. It should be rare, loud and rotated after use.'),
 ('Chain test', 'A series of links an attacker needs. The test records which link each control stops.'),
 ('Consumer', 'An application or job that uses a secret. Change the consumer before the secret.'),
 ('Control', 'A rule or check meant to stop a failure.'),
 ('Front door', 'The place where new identities are created or approved, and where the wrong ones can be refused.'),
 ('Ghost credential', 'A key or account that nobody owns and nobody remembers.'),
 ('Guess file', 'The written expectations for a group of cases. It is hashed and committed before any code is written.'),
 ('Hash (SHA-256)', 'A 64-character fingerprint of a file. Change one character in the file and the fingerprint changes.'),
 ('Just-in-time (JIT) access', 'Access granted for a short window when it is needed and removed when the window ends.'),
 ('Limit', 'What a control cannot see. Every case should have one.'),
 ('Masked', 'Switching a control off alone changed nothing, because another control covered it or it did not matter in that case.'),
 ('Noticed', 'Switching that one control off changed a result.'),
 ('Non-human identity (NHI)', 'An account or credential used by software and not by a person: a service account, API key, token, certificate, workload or agent.'),
 ('OAuth grant', 'Permission a person or organisation gives an app to act on their data, usually through a token.'),
 ('Replay', 'Using a stolen token again from somewhere else.'),
 ('Roll forward', 'Issue a new value, move users to it, and only then remove the old one.'),
 ('Service account', 'An account an application or job uses to sign in.'),
 ('Sponsor', 'The person accountable for a vendor or agent identity, who is contacted if there is an incident.'),
 ('Tier', 'A rating of how much damage an identity can do. Tier 0 can control identity systems or all of production, Tier 1 reaches production data or systems, Tier 2 reaches little. These tiers are a proposal. Your organisation sets the thresholds.'),
 ('Wrong guess', 'A number or a ranking in my guess that did not equal the result. The book keeps both.'),
]

